+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS=1, the frame-ahead guard's copies serve every GPU-side block read and span of guest memory (port of yuri2301/Eglantine c5145ace9), off by default
+
+Upstream: yuri2301/Eglantine branch pitoco, commit c5145ace9bea5ca3325b6e7e82970bcf11e6d3e3
+(yuri2301, 11 Nov 2026, "Ocarina of Time: frame overlap copies when running a frame ahead").
+Credit for the idea and the read sites: yuri2301.
+
+What upstream does: running a frame ahead, the game's first write to a page the frame in flight
+may still read saves a 4 KiB copy first; GPU-side reads (DeviceMemoryManager::ReadBlock,
+ReadBlockUnsafe, GetSpan, Tegra::MemoryManager::ReadBlockImpl, the buffer cache's direct
+pointers) put the copies over what they read until the frame's fence, where the copies go and
+their memory is marked written. PC, village spawn point: 44 -> 31.5 ms a frame, no flashes in 450 frames.
+
+What we had: EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=2/3 (live =3 in the play settings) is the same mechanism with
+its own trap, pool, slots and held writes, but its copies serve the buffer cache only (uploads,
+streamed uniforms, ReadGpu handles/pointers, the direct-pointer paths via HasCopy). Its header
+said "Not covered: texture data and descriptor tables the texture cache reads". This patch ports
+the part we lacked, on top of our guard, not upstream's second guard:
+
+EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS=1 (needs EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=2 or 3; read once; a warning line
+otherwise):
+ - DeviceMemoryManager::ReadBlock / ReadBlockUnsafe: after the read, AheadGuard::Overlay puts the
+   copy of each page copied for a frame the back still records over the bytes (after, as
+   upstream: a write that copies its page during the read is still covered);
+ - Tegra::MemoryManager::ReadBlockImpl (both page kinds) and the small ReadBlockUnsafe path
+   (descriptors): the same per device piece;
+ - DeviceMemoryManager::GetSpan (both): no span over a range with a copy, so GpuGuestMemory and
+   other callers read it by block;
+ - what a block read took from a copy goes on the slot's `served` list, so it is handed back as a
+   guest write when that frame is passed or lifted (TakeRedirty): a texture uploaded from a copy
+   is uploaded again from memory;
+ - implies EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_WRITES=1 unless that is set (upstream copies every page the
+   caches hold that the game writes; ALL_WRITES is ours for that).
+A thread-local mark keeps the guard's own reads (a copy being taken, Read's live part) from
+re-entering Overlay (no second lock, no copy over a new copy's source).
+
+Line, with the guard's 300-present window:
+"EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS: last 300 presents (to #<n>): <n> device block reads and <n>
+GPU-address block reads took <KiB> KiB from copies, <n> spans refused for a copy".
+Zero there means the extra sites never met a copy (upstream found all its hits in buffer
+uploads, which our guard already covered): then the switch cannot be what fixes a flash.
+
+Off: one cached bool test per block read and span. Not in the kept-store stamp: ahead_guard.h,
+memory_manager.cpp, device_memory_manager.inc are no translation id inputs. KEEPS THE STORE.
