+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW fix, only the split's back skips break adds (checker fix to 1005)
+
+Fix to 1005's port of lucastaonline's 865afaa4f3 (#1161), as taken into zortos293/Lichii
+5e428570d2 (PR #1586, Zortos (zortos293) with capy-ai).
+
+With EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW=1, any thread that called Nx2FastDraw::Serial() became a "reader" whose
+breaks skip the locked add once it has bumped the serial since its last read. The GPU thread
+draws (and reads the serial in PrepareDraw) before GpuSplit::MaybeStart starts the back; after
+that it is the front, reads the serial no more, and so would skip every break after its first for
+the rest of the session. A front break between two back draws then leaves the serial unchanged and
+the back's next draw takes a stale delta (wrong picture). Now only the thread GpuSplit::BackLoop
+marks (the back, the only thread whose draws can be reused: Ineligible::OffBackThread) re-arms in
+Serial(); every other thread always adds, as without the switch. Without the split nothing is a
+reader. Unset: as before. No translation id input: KEEPS THE STORE.
