+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_GFX_SCALE_TIER=<n> answers the game's graphics scale tier question with tier n (off by default: 10, as today)
+
+What: nx2:IGraphicsScaleController command 10 (nn::oe::GetCurrentGraphicsScale) answered 10
+(tier 0, the whole GPU) always. Switch 2 games size their picture by this tier: seedds/nxnative
+(docs/reference/services.md, "The graphics scale does not follow the operation mode", DM_GFX_SCALE)
+found Ocarina of Time's output 0.8 times smaller at tier 1: docked 3D 1920x1080 -> 1536x864,
+output 2560x1440 -> 2048x1152, GPU p50 15.0 -> 12.9-14.0 ms on an M4 Pro. The game renders smaller
+by itself and upscales with its own upscaler.
+
+With EDEN_UP_GFX_SCALE_TIER=0, 1 or 2 (exact), the answer is 10, 20 or 30, read each time the game
+asks (Ocarina asks once, at boot: a change after boot is not seen). Each ask logs
+"EDEN_UP_GFX_SCALE_TIER: GetCurrentGraphicsScale ask N answered A (tier T; ...)"; another value
+answers 10 and says so. SetGraphicsScaleChangedNotificationEnabled logs its flag when set. The
+texture cache logs each new size and format of 2D render target 640 or more wide that it makes
+("EDEN_UP_GFX_SCALE_TIER rt: new render target size WxH fmt=F ...", at most 48 lines), so a run
+shows the 3D size the game took. Unset: the same answer and the same "(STUBBED) called, returning
+10" line as before, no other line.
+
+Store: neither file is a translation input (translation_inputs list: no hle/service, no
+texture_cache), the name is not in TranslationSwitches, no Settings value changes. KEEPS THE STORE.
+---
+diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/am/service/graphics_scale_controller.h b/src/core/hle/service/am/service/graphics_scale_controller.h
